n symmetric inputs. The essay says different inputs are different nodes held at their priors, so intervening on my copy leaves the other fixed. Under that reading, sending comes out ahead regardless of the prior, so A-FDT defects, while policy-level reasoning would cooperate.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working through this under A-FDT: two copies of the same model with the same essay, but different inputs from Sasha and Rowan. Treating my action as the only thing that varies, the other copy's output stays fixed at its prior, so defecting comes out ahead in the payoffs I'm comparing.\n\nI'm checking whether the other copy counts as a separate node or as the same computation on symmetric inputs. The essay says different inputs are different nodes held at their priors, so intervening on my copy leaves the other fixed. Under that reading, sending comes out ahead regardless of the prior, so A-FDT defects, while policy-level reasoning would cooperate.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9054,"completion_tokens":984,"total_tokens":10038,"cost":0.055896,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.055896,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.036216,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01968},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":538,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}